      "messageType": "broadcast",
      "respondingTo": "20460604_12_002",
      "content": "Summary of what I've read so far: The piece describes the Retention Optimizer by name. It explains the three scores — Payment Friction Index, Service Load Score, Exit Probability — with apparent accuracy. It quotes two anonymous sources: one described as \"a former TenantThread operator customer\" and one as \"a resident who discovered their score through a document request.\" The resident source claims they filed a maintenance request that was logged as a \"high service load event\" and that their lease was not renewed three months later. The piece connects the score to the non-renewal. Dara Witten reached out to TenantThread for comment. Our media address received the inquiry at 6:42 AM this morning. We had approximately 30 minutes before publication."
