      "content": "Outside counsel was already briefed for this scenario. The primary flag: if TenantThread discloses the merger while under active negative press coverage of its core product, the acquirer will want representations that there are no undisclosed material liabilities related to the data practices issue. We'll need a clean reps and warranties pass. That is possible but it takes 24–48 hours of document review. If you want to announce by Friday, we need to start that review tonight. Second flag: the AG inquiries — both state offices may view an acquisition announcement as an attempt to complicate their oversight. I'd recommend preemptive disclosure to both AG offices before the public announcement. I can handle that. Tell me the timeline and I'll move."
