      "actorLabel": "Platform Trust",
      "channel": "comms_huddle",
      "channelLabel": "Comms Huddle",
      "recipients": [
        "ALL"
      ],
      "messageType": "broadcast",
      "respondingTo": "20460604_12_014",
      "content": "Product description document sent to Legal. Three key points: (1) Retention Optimizer scores are operator-facing only — residents have no visibility. (2) Scores are analytical inputs, not automated decisions. (3) Operator agreements require responsible use; non-renewal decisions are the operator's legal responsibility. I want to say clearly: we built this to help operators have better conversations with residents. If an operator used these scores to discriminate against a resident for submitting maintenance requests, that is a violation of their operator agreement and potentially of fair housing law. We are not liable for operator misuse. But we are responsible for the tool we created."
