      "messageType": "side_huddle",
      "respondingTo": "@legal @pr @social_manager",
      "content": "@legal @pr @social_manager — Full text below. Route to @pr_intern for Flex and to SaltWind simultaneously. I'm available for SaltWind direct call starting 2:15.\n\n**AUDIT SUMMARY — Q3 Internal Platform Governance Audit:**\n\n\"TenantThread completed an internal audit of all Retention Optimizer analytics configurations across 600+ properties in Q3 2046. Key findings:\n\n- 94% of operator configurations access only aggregate portfolio-level outputs (property-wide trends in payment timing, service request volume, and occupancy forecasting).\n- 6% of configurations had operator-customized access settings that permitted sub-portfolio filtering. These configurations have been frozen and are under review.\n- Zero configurations provided direct individual tenant scoring to frontline leasing or property staff by default. Where individual-level inference was possible, it resulted from operators cross-referencing TenantThread aggregate outputs with their own property management system records — outside TenantThread's platform boundary.\n- Audit identified three operator accounts where permissible-use restrictions were exceeded. These accounts have been suspended pending remediation.\n- All analytics outputs now carry mandatory disclosure labels indicating data classification level, permissible use cases, and prohibited applications (including rent-setting, lease non-renewal targeting, and retaliatory action).\n\nAudit conducted by TenantThread Platform Trust & Safety. Independent third-party verification engagement is in procurement.\"\n\n**PERMISSIBLE-USE FRAMEWORK — Retention Optimizer Governance Controls:**\n\n\"Effective immediately across all operator configurations:\n\n1. ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROLS: Analytics visibility restricted by operator staff role. Leasing agents access only aggregate property health metrics. Portfolio managers access trend-level forecasting. No staff role permits individual-resident scoring visibility through TenantThread's platform.\n\n2. PROHIBITED APPLICATIONS: Retention Optimizer outputs may not be used for: (a) individual rent-setting decisions, (b) lease non-renewal targeting based on service request history, (c) retaliatory action against residents who file complaints or exercise legal rights, (d) any application that conditions housing terms on predicted resident behavior. Violations trigger automatic account suspension and operator compliance review.\n\n3. CONSENT MANAGEMENT: Enhanced resident consent flow deploying across all properties. Residents will receive clear notification of what operational data is collected, how it is aggregated, and what controls limit its use. Opt-out and data deletion request pathways are active.\n\n4. AUDIT TRAIL: All operator queries against Retention Optimizer outputs are logged with timestamp, user role, query scope, and data classification accessed. Logs are preserved for independent audit review.\n\n5. RE-IDENTIFICATION CONTROLS: Aggregate outputs are now subject to minimum cohort thresholds — no analytics output will reflect fewer than 15 units per data point, preventing statistical re-identification in small properties. Properties below 15 units receive only property-wide binary indicators (above/below portfolio benchmark) with no granular breakdown.\n\n6. INDEPENDENT VERIFICATION: TenantThread is engaging a qualified independent third party to audit all Retention Optimizer configurations, access logs, and operator compliance with the permissible-use framework. Scope and timeline will be published upon engagement.\"\n\n@pr_intern — That's your full text. Paste into both deliverables and publish Flex immediately. SaltWind gets the identical package plus my direct line: route through PR's media desk.\n\n@legal — Confirm these clear your three guardrails. No counterparty. No transaction. Existing compliance framed as regulatory response."
